  "body": "The Sodick wire post of issue 617 writes no tank, flushing or wire-drive words: its header says \"TANK FILL AND FLUSHING ARE NOT PROGRAMMED - SET THEM AT THE CONTROL\". The 1998 \"Wire EDM Machine Operation\" manual (Mark 21 / EX21) lists them (T84 high-pressure flush, T85 low-pressure flush, T94 submerged, T89 non-submerged, T80 / T81 wire drive, T82 / T83 drain, T86 / T87 pump, T96 / T97 fill pump) and its example writes T94, T91, T84 before the cut.\n\nWanted: the operation (or the machine file) states what the job needs - submerged or not, high or low flushing - and the post writes the matching T words at the right place around threading and cutting; nothing is written when nothing is stated. Each new parameter is an undoable command with its MCP tool.\n\nDone means: a Wire Contour with flushing and submerged cutting stated posts the T words in the manual's order to a new golden; one that states nothing posts as today; an unknown choice is refused by name.\n\nPart of #617\n",
